---
What a cron expression means, and when it runs next

Usage: tw cron [OPTIONS] [VALUE]

Arguments:
  [VALUE]  The input itself; stdin when left out, or -

Options:
  -n, --next <N>            How many of the next runs to list
      --tz <TEXT>           The zone the schedule runs in; this computer's when left out
      --relative-to <TEXT>  List the runs after this moment; now when left out
  -i, --input <FILE>        Read the input from FILE
      --json                Write the result as JSON
      --no-newline          Do not end text output with a newline
  -h, --help                Print help
